<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><em><span style=3D"font-size: 14px; font-weig=
ht: normal;">(Vay)</span></em><span style=3D"font-weight: bold; font-size: =
22px;"><br><br>The weird way this rental startup delivers its cars</span><b=
r><br>If you were asked to imagine a driverless car, you=E2=80=99d probably=
 think of:</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li aria-level=3D"1">An autonomous vehicle, like a Waymo<br><br></li>
<li aria-level=3D"1">A situation that=E2=80=99s gone very awry</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">With Vay, a Berlin-based startup that offers =
on-demand car rentals in Las Vegas, it means a third thing: remotely contro=
lled cars. <br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><span style=3D"font-weight: bold; font-size: =
18px;">How does that work?</span><br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Vay=E2=80=99s fleet consists of 100 Kia Niro&=
nbsp;SUVs, <a href=3D"https://media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VWH=
1Vm3GKCTWW7kCBzG3nl8_fW52hptB5JMHD1N70Sktx2-ZW0W7Y8-PT6lZ3pDW7PtyCD5tJq71W1=
fplf18xNRv0W1NGGRn9fqpLyW59jyHx4pmNz9W4PP6BM68gFwMW5GbBMc3bGgNkW9kF98T4vlmv=
-W51nB6K3KhmXxW3KThFG6Gm-7_W1FNVM23k341RMzMh2Y2DBTjV8lSnz6tV99VW7wKhRG6Mqqh=
qVYhmbg8Jbk0ZW4KM7yH7DvqcdW4qLSNX7C4ry5W2JxdVP6W5XSVW4B11qB3JhQvQW1pmfRj3Jh=
7xvW2n8sTg3SFZG9MBx0rWGTRz9W56l4q92j6L_jW3Drmfm85k5QvW4NtBdw53_2H-W5ZDp_j5c=
X_VJW7t-lCt5KNcSMf34m5P804" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" d=
ata-hs-link-id-v2=3D"+cZWVTig" target=3D"_blank">per</a> <span style=3D"fon=
t-style: italic;">Business Insider</span>, which customers can order throug=
h its app.&nbsp;</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li style=3D"line-height: 150%;">
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Customers can pick up their car themselves, o=
r a remote driver =E2=80=94 a human sitting in Vay=E2=80=99s office in fron=
t of several monitors, a steering wheel, and pedals =E2=80=94 can pilot it&=
nbsp;to the customer.</p>
&nbsp;</li>
<li style=3D"line-height: 150%;">
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Once a customer receives the car, they take o=
ver driving and the remote driver is disconnected. Customers return cars in=
 designated service zones or hand them back off to remote drivers.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Vincent Reddy, an operations lead, told<em> B=
I </em>that Vay=E2=80=99s remote driving setup is similar to a =E2=80=9Chig=
h-grade racing sim=E2=80=9D but without the ability to feel the road or the=
 car=E2=80=99s movement. <br><br>Unlike autonomous vehicles, which often us=
e LiDAR to navigate, Vay uses only cameras. It=E2=80=99s a lot cheaper, and=
 a human =E2=80=94&nbsp;not a bot =E2=80=94 remains in control.&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><br>Vay=E2=80=99s cars can=E2=80=99t drive ov=
er 25 mph until renters take over, and if there=E2=80=99s an emergency, rem=
ote drivers can push a red button to pull over.&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><br><span style=3D"font-weight: bold; font-si=
ze: 18px;">Who uses this service?</span> <br><br>Vay=E2=80=99s been operati=
ng in Vegas <a href=3D"https://media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VW=
H1Vm3GKCTWW7kCBzG3nl8_fW52hptB5JMHD1N70Sktx2-ZW0W7Y8-PT6lZ3mgW3Y3xdv4GslHFW=
6Wx0rc1p4gMFW68Ppzg1mtj4CW6Dw8h65JzWyWW4mttHV7QxDG4W2dJkSb6RR6VxW7dPwPf4pdW=
ftW2l4H-C5f076pW3cdrrS1s0KxDW8pN5PT5Xh8m0W6kzJnW972vxXW81t6pX8-sV0ZW90FC1j4=
4DnFsW4GrwzJ99Jr86W7VhGW04HH5dqW2tlv8053lxVWW5495RK8VQqcvMrJ8sqzvS1DW6RsVYR=
1Kxm9QW2DxHF59jbVX2W9bfXlh4QfvpZW1dRZhh63Qqf9W3wpZRr9fFLg7W31hPQT3Rz7b7W3f2=
_zb1zL7vNW8034wv87gCBzf2Rdy0d04" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D=
"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"PCLODJiD" target=3D"_blank">since January 2024 </=
a>and says it has provided 35k trips since its founding.&nbsp;<br><br>Vay a=
ims to be cheaper and more convenient than Uber, charging 35 cents per minu=
te while driving and 5 cents per minute&nbsp;while parked.<br><br><span sty=
le=3D"font-style: italic;">The Las Vegas Review-Journal </span><a href=3D"h=
